WEBVTT

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:02.350
Well, let's get crackin'.

00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:03.580
Let's-a-go.

00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:05.920
Stop messing around and start!

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:34.650
Miyuki-san!

00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:37.280
Got any plans for the end of the year?

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:39.220
Izumi-san.

00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:42.760
There's this festival and I was
wondering if you'd like to go...

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:44.700
A festival for the end of the year?

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:46.330
Sounds like fun.

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.080
It'll be lots of fun!

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:51.880
Is it something like a snow festival?

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:54.300
But I'm going to visit relatives...

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:55.920
Pretty sure that...

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:59.550
...I received a similar invitation back during summer.

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:00.640
Kagami-san.

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:02.810
I'll translate what Konata said.

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:06.020
She wants buddies to buy stuff for her at Comic Market.

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:08.080
I was totally freaked out by the site when I went.

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:09.810
I'm not lying.

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:11.630
A festival's a festival.

00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:14.040
It's all work and no fun by yourself.

00:02:17.050 --> 00:02:19.220
Heisei 18
Dec
Heisei 18
Dec

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:19.880
Hello?

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:21.380
This is the Izumi residence.

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:23.350
Konata?

00:02:23.350 --> 00:02:25.220
I'm writing New Year's cards right now.

00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:26.950
Are you guys in mourning and refusing cards?

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:28.720
Didn't get a letter about it...

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:30.600
No.

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:31.940
Where did that come from?

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:33.060
Well, you know...

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:36.920
Weren't you absent one day this
year because of a death in the family?

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:39.730
Um...

00:02:41.450 --> 00:02:42.850
But don't worry about that.

00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:45.320
Don't tell me you used another trick out of manga?!

00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:46.160
Shiny shine!

00:02:46.490 --> 00:02:49.040
I'm in the middle of cleaning right now.

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:50.580
I see.

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:52.040
Then I won't keep you.

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:53.060
I'll hang up.

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:54.450
Bye!

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:04.760
I wonder why...

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:10.140
When there's something you don't
want to do, you suddenly want to clean...

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:14.460
...but once you start cleaning, it suddenly feels like a pain?

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:15.480
Konata.

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:16.940
Less resting, okay?

00:03:23.990 --> 00:03:25.830
It's called Comiket?

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:27.810
I heard it was a big festival...

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:30.310
...but it sure starts early.

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:31.730
I'm so excited!

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:34.290
Looks like you haven't heard anything.

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:35.360
Poor thing.

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:36.210
Nah.

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:37.500
She'll get used to it soon enough.

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:38.400
Tsukasa...

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:39.110
Just so you know...

00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:40.780
...this event is gonna exhaust you...

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:42.070
...in more than one way...

00:03:42.070 --> 00:03:42.820
Will you be okay?

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:45.450
Then I'll do my best!

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:47.340
Do you really understand?

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:02.410
<i>Picking up more and more of her people...</i>

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:13.600
Okay!

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:15.830
You'll soon be allowed to enter!

00:04:16.170 --> 00:04:17.040
Sis...

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:18.860
This place is kinda scary...

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:20.290
Told you...

00:04:22.070 --> 00:04:22.800
That's right.

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:25.340
I should explain your assignments now.

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:26.550
Assignments?

00:04:26.550 --> 00:04:27.490
Here you go.

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:29.120
These are your shopping lists.

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:35.100
Once we get inside, we'll split up and go
around the circles according to this map.

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:37.710
You two handle 1-3 in the east building.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.730
I'll take 4-6.

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:41.460
But be careful.

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:43.420
If you don't follow the path marked in red...

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:45.610
...you might get stuck between rows of displays...

00:04:45.610 --> 00:04:48.120
...and end up trapped.

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:49.680
And here and here...

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:51.350
If you're swept into the crowd there...

00:04:51.350 --> 00:04:53.730
...you'll be stuck for over half an hour.

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:56.790
Why do we have to work so hard?

00:04:56.790 --> 00:04:57.960
Just do it.

00:04:58.420 --> 00:05:02.210
The ones marked with green can wait until afternoon.

00:05:02.210 --> 00:05:04.470
They're stocked up...

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:06.570
...so there's almost no danger of them running out.

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:09.850
Just focus on the ones marked in red before noon.

00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:10.970
S stands for something newly published.

00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:12.390
K stands for something already in print.

00:05:12.390 --> 00:05:16.220
If you don't know what's what, just buy everything.

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:17.830
Here's your ammo.

00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:20.790
You're going to have to pay in cash.

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:22.920
The coffee will be your only refreshment for a while.

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:24.550
Take a drink every thirty minutes.

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:26.930
This will be our final rendezvous point.

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:28.470
1 PM on the dot.

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:30.550
I'll wait fifteen minutes...

00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:31.350
...but if you don't show up...

00:05:31.370 --> 00:05:34.100
...I'll go look for you in the medical office so watch the clock.

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:34.770
That is all.

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:35.490
Any questions?

00:05:35.490 --> 00:05:36.670
You only ever sound...

00:05:36.670 --> 00:05:40.870
...intelligent and passionate when this kind of stuff is involved.

00:05:42.090 --> 00:05:43.380
Please don't run!

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:44.670
Climax from the beginning!

00:05:45.170 --> 00:05:49.340
The limit for new works is four copies per person.

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:50.620
Please cooperate.

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:53.490
Um...

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:54.580
Excuse me.

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:56.910
This is A-92, right?

00:05:56.910 --> 00:05:57.870
Yes.

00:05:58.330 --> 00:06:00.040
One of each new book?

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:01.250
That will be 1,000 yen.

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:02.110
Yes, what did you need?

00:06:02.110 --> 00:06:03.130
Um...

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:05.210
Which of these are new...

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:05.710
Yes.

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:07.470
The new ones would be this and this.

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:08.680
Each one is 500 yen.

00:06:09.130 --> 00:06:10.340
Good work!

00:06:10.340 --> 00:06:13.350
Did you enjoy the snacks?

00:06:13.350 --> 00:06:14.430
That's wonderful!

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:15.350
U-Um...

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:16.680
Three of each please.

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:17.700
Thank you for your business!

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:19.400
Dripping Brigade Chief...

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:20.850
...and Naughty Captain, correct?

00:06:20.850 --> 00:06:22.670
Your total comes to 3,000 yen!

00:06:25.460 --> 00:06:26.570
I'd like these.

00:06:26.570 --> 00:06:26.990
Okay.

00:06:27.010 --> 00:06:28.650
Your total is 4,500 yen.

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:29.430
Here.

00:06:29.430 --> 00:06:30.950
Thank you very much!

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:40.460
Locked and loaded...

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:42.180
Onto the next point.

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:43.290
Um...

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:44.670
Is this the east building?

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:47.590
Then north should be this way...

00:06:47.590 --> 00:06:48.300
Um...

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:49.260
Wa—

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:52.120
Excuse me!

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:53.360
I'm going that way!

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:57.850
I've pretty much covered all the big places.

00:06:57.850 --> 00:06:58.680
Let's see...

00:06:58.680 --> 00:07:00.100
The next place is...

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:14.830
<i>Just a peek...</i>

00:07:17.830 --> 00:07:19.910
<i>Gauron and Sousuke are...</i>

00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:23.380
<i>This is...</i>

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:24.980
Would you like that?

00:07:24.980 --> 00:07:26.710
It'll be 500 yen.

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:28.550
Um...

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:29.800
Too intense for me!

00:07:33.280 --> 00:07:34.260
She's here.

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:35.180
It's her.

00:07:35.180 --> 00:07:36.740
Legendary Girl A!

00:07:36.990 --> 00:07:37.740
Calm down.

00:07:37.740 --> 00:07:39.890
She'll think we're weird if we panic.

00:07:40.870 --> 00:07:42.750
But there's a weird jinx...

00:07:42.750 --> 00:07:46.820
...where every circle suddenly
becomes big after she buys a book!

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:48.980
It's impossible to stay calm!

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:49.940
I know!

00:07:49.940 --> 00:07:52.490
That's why we put so much effort into this book!

00:07:52.490 --> 00:07:54.010
So she would buy it!

00:07:54.260 --> 00:07:55.930
You're right...

00:07:55.930 --> 00:07:57.060
Even though it was the end of the year...

00:07:57.060 --> 00:07:59.430
...we skipped work to do this!

00:07:59.430 --> 00:08:01.160
This year will be our year!

00:08:01.160 --> 00:08:02.250
Can I take a look?

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:03.570
Yes! Go ahead!

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:15.320
Uh...

00:08:15.320 --> 00:08:16.570
What do you think?

00:08:16.570 --> 00:08:20.320
We put a lot of work into the concert scene.

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:23.290
Iffy.

00:08:23.620 --> 00:08:25.230
Thankssomuch.

00:08:29.190 --> 00:08:30.150
Don't cry!

00:08:30.150 --> 00:08:31.250
Next summer for sure!

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:33.490
Um...

00:08:33.490 --> 00:08:34.570
Excuse me.

00:08:34.570 --> 00:08:35.110
Yes?

00:08:35.110 --> 00:08:36.280
What's the matter?

00:08:36.280 --> 00:08:40.160
Where is Pu-61 located?

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:40.830
Pu?

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:43.080
Wasn't Pu in the east building?

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:44.970
Where is the east building?

00:08:45.230 --> 00:08:46.690
This is the west building.

00:08:46.690 --> 00:08:48.060
If you want to go to the east building...

00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:49.440
...get in that line there...

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:51.010
...and go up one floor.

00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:53.610
How long will it take?

00:08:53.610 --> 00:08:54.570
Let's see...

00:08:54.570 --> 00:08:56.720
At this time, probably an hour.

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:03.450
<i>Okay, I'm done.</i>

00:09:05.580 --> 00:09:07.560
Sorry, Kona-chan.

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:11.130
I just now got back from the west building.

00:09:11.460 --> 00:09:15.090
You get completely lost after
getting caught up in the crowd...

00:09:15.090 --> 00:09:16.510
...in this event...

00:09:16.510 --> 00:09:19.470
I had to wait in line for an hour to use the restroom.

00:09:19.470 --> 00:09:19.870
Well...

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:23.770
I figured it would be a rough schedule for a first-timer...

00:09:23.770 --> 00:09:26.920
...so let's just stroll around for the afternoon.

00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:28.630
<i>You're not done yet?</i>

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:29.710
But you know...

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:34.240
...it's gotten a lot better since they moved this to Ariake.

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:38.870
They only had two convenience stores near the site at Harumi.

00:09:38.870 --> 00:09:40.370
Site at Harumi?

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:44.750
The last one at Harumi was twelve years ago, huh?

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:45.430
Wait.

00:09:45.430 --> 00:09:47.230
How old were you?

00:09:47.230 --> 00:09:48.440
Around five?

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:50.750
My dad took me.

00:09:51.090 --> 00:09:54.360
We always stayed at this place called Hotel Urashima.

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:56.570
My first time was at the summer festival.

00:09:56.570 --> 00:09:59.620
That was one crazy second floor.

00:09:59.620 --> 00:10:02.740
The sweat from all the participants evaporated...

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:05.500
...and turned into these fluffy steam clouds.

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:06.270
Enough already.

00:10:06.270 --> 00:10:07.310
Don't want to hear it.

00:10:07.600 --> 00:10:11.900
Everything's gotten a lot easier
after they moved this to Ariake...

00:10:11.900 --> 00:10:14.030
...but maybe it's 'cause of the
people mainly here for events...

00:10:14.030 --> 00:10:19.570
...many of the younger participants think
of themselves as customers, sadly enough.

00:10:20.030 --> 00:10:23.060
This was supposed to be an event put on by all of us.

00:10:23.060 --> 00:10:25.270
Sorry to interrupt you while you're on a roll...

00:10:25.270 --> 00:10:26.280
...but you've totally lost me.

00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:33.730
I didn't come here during summer...

00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:33.940
...but they also have places like these, huh?

00:10:33.940 --> 00:10:34.610
There.

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:35.530
...but they also have places like these, huh?

00:10:36.110 --> 00:10:38.950
The main stuff is probably all sold out though.

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:41.880
It's Nagato! Nagato!

00:10:42.030 --> 00:10:42.700
The person behind Nagamon is here as a salesgirl!

00:10:42.700 --> 00:10:43.450
Here.

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:44.640
Thank you very much.

00:10:44.640 --> 00:10:45.830
What are you talking about?

00:10:45.830 --> 00:10:48.600
How can you be out of Haruhi goods?!

00:10:48.600 --> 00:10:51.430
Why did I bother coming here if the
Nagato phone cards are sold out?!

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:52.420
Please calm down!

00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:53.040
He's horrible.

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:53.500
I can't do anything about it!

00:10:53.500 --> 00:10:54.210
Like I just said.

00:10:54.210 --> 00:10:55.050
Like I care!

00:10:55.050 --> 00:10:55.170
There's been a spike in people like him.

00:10:55.170 --> 00:10:57.190
I'm never coming back to this dump!
There's been a spike in people like him.

00:10:57.530 --> 00:11:00.200
I'm terribly sorry, sir!

00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:02.370
Unfortunately, our limited goods...

00:11:02.370 --> 00:11:04.110
...have already sold out!

00:11:05.040 --> 00:11:07.000
Really?!

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:08.830
Well, if you're gonna show up this late.

00:11:08.830 --> 00:11:09.120
Figured as much.

00:11:09.440 --> 00:11:10.520
I feel for you...

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:12.000
...but you gotta line up early...

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:13.660
Fool!

00:11:14.670 --> 00:11:15.500
Asia...

00:11:17.300 --> 00:11:18.210
Wh-What?!

00:11:18.420 --> 00:11:20.180
Even customers who show up late...

00:11:20.180 --> 00:11:22.140
...must be completely satisfied!

00:11:22.140 --> 00:11:24.220
Have you lost the true spirit?

00:11:24.220 --> 00:11:25.560
B-But...

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:28.510
All we have is leftover stuff now!

00:11:30.020 --> 00:11:31.640
Leftover, you say?

00:11:33.810 --> 00:11:36.020
Leftover items still have value!

00:11:37.790 --> 00:11:39.280
A value that can't be found...

00:11:39.280 --> 00:11:41.530
...in popular items and mainstream turn-ons!

00:11:41.530 --> 00:11:45.200
This Comiket exists to reveal their true value!

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:48.100
Now that all limited goods have been eliminated...

00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:51.600
...the true battle has begun for industry booths!

00:11:52.920 --> 00:11:54.830
B-By George...

00:11:54.830 --> 00:11:55.500
Now!

00:11:55.500 --> 00:11:57.550
Make a recommendation to the customer!

00:11:57.550 --> 00:11:59.970
Dig up your true item!

00:12:01.170 --> 00:12:02.990
Anything I can use as a weapon?

00:12:05.100 --> 00:12:05.800
Ho—

00:12:05.840 --> 00:12:07.300
How about this?!

00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:08.310
No!

00:12:08.310 --> 00:12:09.600
Gotta be this!

00:12:09.810 --> 00:12:10.520
No, you see.

00:12:10.520 --> 00:12:12.060
Nagato and everybody else is selling like hotcakes...

00:12:12.060 --> 00:12:13.310
...yet look at this.

00:12:13.310 --> 00:12:15.020
Even Koizumi's sells well.

00:12:15.020 --> 00:12:15.650
Quiet!

00:12:15.650 --> 00:12:17.730
This one's gone unsold for three years!

00:12:17.730 --> 00:12:19.610
And the Captain's sold out instantly!

00:12:19.610 --> 00:12:21.610
So please purchase this Kyon!

00:12:21.780 --> 00:12:23.660
No, I recommend Sousuke!

00:12:23.660 --> 00:12:25.490
No, I wanted CoCo Saikoubi-chan!

00:12:25.490 --> 00:12:27.240
You...

00:12:27.240 --> 00:12:29.450
...fools!

00:12:32.330 --> 00:12:33.500
Y-You're...

00:12:33.500 --> 00:12:34.540
President Takahashi!

00:12:34.850 --> 00:12:35.580
Yes.

00:12:35.580 --> 00:12:36.540
I am...

00:12:36.540 --> 00:12:38.210
...Takahashi the President!

00:12:38.420 --> 00:12:40.920
I overheard your conversation!

00:12:41.150 --> 00:12:42.050
Your desire to promote a new perspecive of value is commendable!

00:12:42.050 --> 00:12:44.320
That place is always pumped up.

00:12:44.320 --> 00:12:45.240
R-Really?
Your desire to promote a new perspecive of value is commendable!

00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:45.990
However...
R-Really?

00:12:45.990 --> 00:12:46.370
R-Really...
However...

00:12:46.370 --> 00:12:50.700
I cannot forgive your selfish desire to promote unpopular characters!

00:12:50.720 --> 00:12:51.250
Well...

00:12:51.250 --> 00:12:52.930
They're both main characters...

00:13:05.950 --> 00:13:08.240
Sis, I'm sleepy.

00:13:08.330 --> 00:13:10.240
I'm sleepy, too.

00:13:10.870 --> 00:13:14.020
We had to help out at home as
soon as we got back from Ariake...

00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:17.450
Why do they have that event on New Year's Eve?

00:13:17.770 --> 00:13:18.440
Kagami.

00:13:18.440 --> 00:13:19.320
Tsukasa.

00:13:19.320 --> 00:13:20.570
Happy New Year!

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:21.900
Kona-chan.

00:13:21.900 --> 00:13:23.740
Happy New Year!

00:13:23.740 --> 00:13:27.240
You have an awful lot of energy for
someone who was at that event since morning.

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:29.530
Plus, it's cold, so I figured you wouldn't bother.

00:13:29.530 --> 00:13:31.450
Well, that's true...

00:13:31.450 --> 00:13:33.950
...but January 1st is a new beginning...

00:13:33.950 --> 00:13:37.710
...so I have to come charge up for the coming year.

00:13:38.420 --> 00:13:39.230
That's admirable.

00:13:39.440 --> 00:13:40.590
No, that's what Dad said.

00:13:40.590 --> 00:13:41.320
Hello!

00:13:41.320 --> 00:13:43.260
<i>Suddenly, I'm disturbed.</i>

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:44.970
Shrine maiden outfits are so invigorating!

00:13:46.940 --> 00:13:48.570
This and that...

00:13:49.030 --> 00:13:50.760
We're done praying.

00:13:50.760 --> 00:13:51.310
Okay.

00:13:51.310 --> 00:13:52.370
Good job.

00:13:52.370 --> 00:13:55.160
Did you guys do any praying?

00:13:55.160 --> 00:13:56.540
Oh, yeah...

00:13:56.540 --> 00:13:58.770
You were doing some intense praying, Sis.

00:13:59.330 --> 00:14:01.270
There you go blabbing again!

00:14:01.270 --> 00:14:03.170
It wasn't that intense.

00:14:03.510 --> 00:14:08.680
I-I was just hoping I could be in the
same class as you and Miyuki this year.

00:14:10.600 --> 00:14:11.470
Sis...

00:14:11.470 --> 00:14:12.430
What about Kona-chan?

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:13.850
You know...

00:14:13.850 --> 00:14:15.600
Kagami's actually pretty cute.

00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:16.500
Be quiet!

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:19.150
You making fun of everything is why I never want to tell you!

00:14:19.150 --> 00:14:21.130
And then there's the way you resist...

00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:22.060
Something wrong with that?!

00:14:22.270 --> 00:14:25.760
Sis has always been the only one in a different class.

00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:29.110
Maybe Ms. Kuroi hates me.

00:14:29.410 --> 00:14:30.370
I'll also pray...

00:14:30.370 --> 00:14:32.660
...to be in the same class...

00:14:32.660 --> 00:14:33.970
...as Sis!

00:14:33.970 --> 00:14:34.820
Tsukasa...

00:14:34.970 --> 00:14:35.770
No way.

00:14:35.770 --> 00:14:38.640
Kagami needs to be in a different class.

00:14:38.640 --> 00:14:39.540
Wh-Why?

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:41.040
'Cause you know...

00:14:41.040 --> 00:14:43.170
That way I can borrow stuff from you when I forget mine.

00:14:43.170 --> 00:14:45.420
And I won't get caught if I copy your homework.

00:14:45.420 --> 00:14:48.570
And if you're in our class, my rank will go down.

00:14:48.570 --> 00:14:50.550
Then you go be in a different class by yourself.

00:14:50.840 --> 00:14:51.450
The other...

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:52.300
The other day...

00:14:52.530 --> 00:14:52.830
Sebastian was...

00:14:52.830 --> 00:14:55.700
<i>Female students are so wonderful...</i>

00:14:57.750 --> 00:15:00.210
Are you going to draw your fortune this year?

00:15:00.210 --> 00:15:01.210
Might as well.

00:15:01.210 --> 00:15:02.230
Since I'm here.

00:15:04.150 --> 00:15:06.780
It's good to get an early start on the year.

00:15:06.780 --> 00:15:07.690
Indeed.

00:15:07.690 --> 00:15:09.320
And I got to see something nice.

00:15:09.320 --> 00:15:11.490
This will be a good year.

00:15:11.490 --> 00:15:13.220
Don't worry.

00:15:13.220 --> 00:15:14.560
If you've already hit rock bottom...

00:15:14.560 --> 00:15:17.220
...things can only get better.

00:15:17.250 --> 00:15:18.430
Something good will happen.

00:15:19.230 --> 00:15:20.390
What can I say...

00:15:20.390 --> 00:15:22.100
It all depends on how you word it.

00:15:22.130 --> 00:15:23.080
Thanks...

00:15:23.420 --> 00:15:26.730
Want to tie a bad luck ward on the tree?

00:15:27.320 --> 00:15:28.470
I'll do that.

00:15:29.590 --> 00:15:30.250
So many!

00:15:31.180 --> 00:15:31.760
Here, too!

00:15:33.010 --> 00:15:34.450
Here's a spot!

00:15:38.600 --> 00:15:40.890
So this is the power of bad luck...

00:15:40.890 --> 00:15:41.850
Looks like it.

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:43.710
Whether or not something good will happen...

00:15:43.710 --> 00:15:46.020
...depends on the amount of effort you spend.

00:15:46.020 --> 00:15:48.530
Drawing your fortune is just a game of luck.

00:15:48.530 --> 00:15:50.650
That's true...

00:15:50.650 --> 00:15:52.760
Although a staff member shouldn't be saying that...

00:15:53.930 --> 00:15:58.180
Maybe I should go for a whole set from very good to very bad.

00:15:58.180 --> 00:16:00.060
Are they supposed to be trading cards?

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:02.520
Maybe you can draw a secret fortune.

00:16:02.520 --> 00:16:05.750
What would a secret fortune be like?

00:16:05.960 --> 00:16:07.520
Like ultra bad luck.

00:16:07.520 --> 00:16:09.130
Why'd you go with something bad?

00:16:09.130 --> 00:16:10.340
Nobody would want that.

00:16:10.340 --> 00:16:11.380
You know...

00:16:11.380 --> 00:16:14.840
Whoever collects all of them gets a special item!

00:16:14.840 --> 00:16:16.300
No, there's no such thing.

00:16:16.490 --> 00:16:17.390
Oh, yeah...

00:16:17.390 --> 00:16:20.730
I just saw a huge kagami mochi...

00:16:20.730 --> 00:16:22.520
This big!

00:16:22.520 --> 00:16:25.000
Is that where your name came from?

00:16:25.580 --> 00:16:27.520
Well, you're not totally wrong...

00:16:27.690 --> 00:16:29.150
The round shape of a kagami mochi...

00:16:29.150 --> 00:16:31.150
...is modeled after a mirror...

00:16:31.150 --> 00:16:35.070
...but it's long been said that gods rest within mirrors...

00:16:35.070 --> 00:16:39.430
...so the name is supposed to
invoke the blessings of the gods.

00:16:40.040 --> 00:16:42.910
And the round shape also signifies family happiness.

00:16:43.080 --> 00:16:45.790
<i>Her name has such a fantastic origin...</i>

00:16:45.790 --> 00:16:49.420
<i>...yet she grew up to be an awfully pragmatic person!</i>

00:16:54.920 --> 00:16:56.160
Would you like one?

00:16:56.160 --> 00:16:56.550
Okay.

00:16:58.560 --> 00:17:00.680
There sure are a lot of worshippers.

00:17:01.040 --> 00:17:03.000
Since it's New Year's.

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:05.170
Though we aren't that well-known.

00:17:09.020 --> 00:17:13.380
I wonder how many of them are
here for the shrine maidens like Dad.

00:17:13.380 --> 00:17:14.680
<i>Here we go again!</i>

00:17:14.680 --> 00:17:16.960
<i>There aren't that many!</i>

00:17:17.430 --> 00:17:18.200
<i>Maybe...</i>

00:17:32.480 --> 00:17:34.110
Then once again...

00:17:34.110 --> 00:17:37.320
Happy New Year!

00:17:37.340 --> 00:17:40.680
Let's have another wonderful year.

00:17:41.010 --> 00:17:41.330
Yeah.

00:17:41.330 --> 00:17:42.040
Let's.

00:17:42.060 --> 00:17:42.910
Hi!

00:17:42.930 --> 00:17:45.160
Happy New Year!

00:17:45.160 --> 00:17:47.080
How about it?

00:17:47.100 --> 00:17:49.230
Look at this beautiful sight!

00:17:49.230 --> 00:17:50.500
Isn't it great?

00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:52.130
Isn't it fantastic?

00:17:52.150 --> 00:17:55.570
Look at all the pretty flowers everywhere!

00:17:59.870 --> 00:18:00.870
Dad.

00:18:00.870 --> 00:18:02.170
Want some tea?

00:18:02.770 --> 00:18:03.660
Sure.

00:18:07.920 --> 00:18:08.690
Here.

00:18:08.690 --> 00:18:10.010
Thanks.

00:18:15.920 --> 00:18:16.680
Dad.

00:18:16.680 --> 00:18:17.550
Want to play a game?

00:18:17.760 --> 00:18:18.550
Dad.

00:18:18.550 --> 00:18:19.550
Want some zoni soup?

00:18:19.800 --> 00:18:20.840
Dad!

00:18:21.300 --> 00:18:22.340
Kinda like that.

00:18:22.640 --> 00:18:28.140
Apparently, he likes how I keep
scurrying over until I get my money.

00:18:28.140 --> 00:18:29.220
I'm exhausted.

00:18:30.150 --> 00:18:31.480
Well, yeah...

00:18:31.480 --> 00:18:33.690
You guys are really close, huh?

00:18:33.840 --> 00:18:36.530
And I managed to get my money...

00:18:36.530 --> 00:18:38.990
...so I'm planning on going to Gamers right now.

00:18:38.990 --> 00:18:40.070
Really...

00:18:40.070 --> 00:18:43.070
The fact that all of those shops are in the city is a pain.

00:18:43.330 --> 00:18:45.950
I'm already on a tight budget.

00:18:45.950 --> 00:18:47.710
And there's the train fee.

00:18:47.710 --> 00:18:50.170
I wish they'd open a shop near us.

00:18:50.170 --> 00:18:54.250
But don't a lot of stores sell online now?

00:18:54.250 --> 00:18:56.710
So you could try that.

00:18:56.880 --> 00:18:58.680
You don't get it...

00:18:58.680 --> 00:19:02.100
You can get points when you order online...

00:19:02.100 --> 00:19:07.270
...but browsing through the store and
making unexpected discoveries is what's really fun.

00:19:07.270 --> 00:19:08.440
What's with you?!

00:19:08.440 --> 00:19:09.810
You're totally ready to spend it all!

00:19:10.080 --> 00:19:12.580
The radishes are almost completely done!

00:19:12.580 --> 00:19:12.980
Now we'll put this completely in.

00:19:12.980 --> 00:19:15.750
I wonder why this is called a pochi bag.

00:19:16.400 --> 00:19:19.070
That's from the phrases pochitto (a
smidge) and korepocchi (just a bit).

00:19:19.070 --> 00:19:21.430
It refers to a bag you put small stuff in.

00:19:22.260 --> 00:19:24.070
Pochitto would be Kansai...

00:19:24.070 --> 00:19:26.310
...and korepocchi would be Kanto.

00:19:32.560 --> 00:19:35.020
Happy New Year!

00:19:35.020 --> 00:19:35.980
This is Takara.

00:19:36.590 --> 00:19:37.420
Miyuki-san.

00:19:37.420 --> 00:19:38.340
Happy New Year!

00:19:38.550 --> 00:19:39.510
Anyway...

00:19:39.510 --> 00:19:42.970
...I was wondering where the name pochi bag came from...

00:19:42.970 --> 00:19:44.070
Pochi bag, is it?
Konata...

00:19:44.070 --> 00:19:45.060
Can't you have a little more faith in your father?

00:19:45.060 --> 00:19:47.120
I believe it came from the phrases pochitto and korepocchi...

00:19:47.120 --> 00:19:48.060
And couldn't you do that somewhere out of sight?

00:19:48.060 --> 00:19:50.350
...and refers to a bag for small items.

00:19:51.500 --> 00:19:52.690
Okay.

00:19:52.690 --> 00:19:57.290
Time to wish everyone in the game a happy new year.

00:20:10.160 --> 00:20:11.190
It's Teacher.

00:20:20.240 --> 00:20:21.710
And like...

00:20:21.880 --> 00:20:24.550
She's always online...

00:20:24.550 --> 00:20:26.930
Doesn't she have anything else to do?

00:20:26.930 --> 00:20:29.010
Guess that's why she doesn't have a boyfriend.

00:20:36.380 --> 00:20:36.920
Go—

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:38.570
Good lucky!

00:20:38.570 --> 00:20:41.220
I'm Akira-sama's assistant, Minoru Shirashi!

00:20:41.220 --> 00:20:44.480
We're already on the twelfth episode of Lucky Channel!

00:20:46.200 --> 00:20:47.830
This sea is hell.

00:20:48.180 --> 00:20:48.930
Uh.

00:20:48.930 --> 00:20:50.200
Yeah...

00:20:50.200 --> 00:20:51.660
As you can see...

00:20:51.660 --> 00:20:54.790
...Akira-sama was supposed to
appear in the actual show this week...

00:20:54.790 --> 00:20:56.730
...but she suddenly became ill...

00:21:02.510 --> 00:21:03.760
A cold, right?

00:21:03.760 --> 00:21:07.220
But I put up a cardboard pop-up instead...

00:21:07.220 --> 00:21:09.500
...so if you go look carefully...

00:21:13.690 --> 00:21:14.330
Hey.

00:21:14.330 --> 00:21:15.290
Akira-sama?

00:21:16.600 --> 00:21:17.810
And so...

00:21:17.810 --> 00:21:20.190
...it looks like Akira-sama's already tired...

00:21:20.190 --> 00:21:22.190
...so we'll have to call it a day!

00:21:22.190 --> 00:21:23.240
Okay, everyone.

00:21:23.240 --> 00:21:24.650
Bye-bee!

00:21:26.240 --> 00:21:29.310
I'm absolutely not getting full of myself.

00:21:30.970 --> 00:21:31.890
I'll?

00:21:31.910 --> 00:21:34.000
Let you hear the new version of <i>Take it! Sailor Uniform</i>?

00:21:34.000 --> 00:21:35.500
So look forward to it?

00:21:35.500 --> 00:21:36.960
If you don't watch next week...

00:21:36.960 --> 00:21:38.710
...I'll turn into Mars and scold you!

00:21:38.710 --> 00:21:39.370
Fumoffu!

00:21:43.760 --> 00:21:45.510
We got pretty into it.

00:21:45.510 --> 00:21:46.800
That was fun.

00:21:47.930 --> 00:21:49.200
Nobody's ordered a song!

00:21:49.200 --> 00:21:51.060
Isn't it your turn?

00:21:51.060 --> 00:21:52.930
Now is when you're supposed to order a song.

00:21:52.930 --> 00:21:54.980
I didn't choose one!

00:21:55.690 --> 00:21:57.770
Which one should I do?

00:21:57.770 --> 00:21:59.110
I'll look, too.

00:21:59.770 --> 00:22:01.190
There's also a menu.

00:22:01.940 --> 00:22:04.070
So you can also eat here.

00:22:04.070 --> 00:22:04.740
Yep.

00:22:04.740 --> 00:22:08.090
That song totally broke my flow.

00:22:08.090 --> 00:22:10.080
Should have saved it for later.

00:22:10.080 --> 00:22:11.450
What flow?

00:22:11.450 --> 00:22:12.740
You know what I mean?

00:22:12.740 --> 00:22:16.250
How you sometimes feel like you sing better?

00:22:16.250 --> 00:22:17.420
No idea.

00:22:17.420 --> 00:22:18.730
Wonder if I can sing this.

00:22:26.340 --> 00:22:28.840
There's a tambourine here.

00:22:28.840 --> 00:22:30.850
We can play it.

00:22:31.470 --> 00:22:32.140
Yuki-chan!

00:22:32.140 --> 00:22:33.200
Try this!

00:22:33.770 --> 00:22:34.790
Sounds nice.

00:22:34.790 --> 00:22:35.450
Okay!

00:22:35.450 --> 00:22:36.100
This one!

00:22:36.100 --> 00:22:37.690
Even a hardcore anime song will work.

00:22:37.690 --> 00:22:38.670
Just go.

00:22:38.670 --> 00:22:41.340
Anyway, I ordered an exciting one.

00:22:44.900 --> 00:22:46.400
You should know this one.

00:22:46.400 --> 00:22:47.300
I do!

00:22:47.300 --> 00:22:48.680
I'll try it.

00:23:11.470 --> 00:23:13.600
Well, next time on Lucky Star:

00:23:13.600 --> 00:23:14.340
I'm Miyuki.

00:23:14.810 --> 00:23:16.730
When something has completely outstripped the competition...

00:23:16.730 --> 00:23:19.000
...and stands heads above the rest...

00:23:19.000 --> 00:23:22.360
...we use the word <i>dantotsu</i> to describe it.

00:23:22.360 --> 00:23:25.480
That's apparently short for <i>danzen</i> (on the very) top.

00:23:25.820 --> 00:23:28.780
This word first appeared in literature...

00:23:28.780 --> 00:23:30.110
...after the recent city election...

00:23:30.110 --> 00:23:33.580
...where that person won by a landslide...

00:23:33.580 --> 00:23:35.470
...on the very top.

00:23:35.470 --> 00:23:36.270
Next time:

00:23:36.270 --> 00:23:37.580
Savory Day.

00:23:37.580 --> 00:23:38.940
Look forward to next time!
